 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Angels carrying the Ark (248:21-22) and the relics of the families of Musa and Harun get no motif and no gloss. burst for the sign; river for the test (not a Paradise river); drop for the single scoop; footsteps for the crossing; mountain for the steadfast. No crowd for the few or the many; the believers' number is not given. STAGING v4: 248: the prophet (blue drop «نبي», always in a wide frame) speaks to the same chiefs (men, uncountable). The Ark, its contents and the angels are not drawn: no plate and no camera toward the sky on 248:9 or 248:21-22; crown plate on 248:5-6, burst on 248:26. 249: Talut (plain man) and his soldiers (uncountable, standing, no fighting) at a river; the soldiers bend to the water on 249:25, then leave the stage on 249:30; the few are 2 figures entering on 249:28, and Talut walks to them on 249:31. The speeches of 249:36-60 get only the camera (the tafsirs differ on who spoke). Jalut is never drawn."
 },
